dzn: Build a 3D view of a 2D image as a 2D view

Vulkan only allows a VK_IMAGE_VIEW_TYPE_3D view of a 3D image. Dozen turns
any 3D view into a D3D12 Texture3D shader resource or unordered access view,
and for a 2D resource that view is an invalid call: D3D12 removes the device
(DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL). Under WSL2 every Vulkan device in the process
shares that ID3D12Device, so gfxstream loses its own device and the Android
VM restarts. 3DMark Wild Life Extreme makes such a view of a 32x32 sRGB
texture each time it starts a second run in one process (RTX 4080 Laptop GPU
and Intel UHD under WSL2); native drivers take it.

Give a 3D view of a 1D or 2D image the 1D or 2D array view the image allows,
and log it once.

--- a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_image.c
+++ b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_image.c
@@ -1003,7 +1003,31 @@
    case VK_COMPONENT_SWIZZLE_A:
       return D3D12_SHADER_COMPONENT_MAPPING_FROM_MEMORY_COMPONENT_3;
    default: UNREACHABLE("Invalid swizzle");
+   }
+}
+
+/* The view type D3D12 can build for the view's image. Vulkan only allows a
+ * 3D view of a 3D image, but an application that asks for one of a 2D image
+ * still works on native drivers, while a D3D12 Texture3D view of a 2D
+ * resource is an invalid call that removes the device, and with it every
+ * other Vulkan device on that ID3D12Device: such a view gets the 2D view the
+ * image does allow.
+ */
+static VkImageViewType
+dzn_image_view_type(const struct dzn_image_view *iview)
+{
+   if (iview->vk.view_type != VK_IMAGE_VIEW_TYPE_3D ||
+       iview->vk.image->image_type == VK_IMAGE_TYPE_3D)
+      return iview->vk.view_type;
+
+   static bool warned;
+   if (!warned) {
+      warned = true;
+      mesa_logw("dzn: a 3D view of a %dD image is created as a 2D view",
+                iview->vk.image->image_type + 1);
    }
+   return iview->vk.image->image_type == VK_IMAGE_TYPE_1D ?
+          VK_IMAGE_VIEW_TYPE_1D_ARRAY : VK_IMAGE_VIEW_TYPE_2D_ARRAY;
 }
 
